# .recur-warp

Purpose: name the desired completed eventness reality first, then compare the
current lane evidence against it.

Warp is the convergence idea: move from primitive setup toward a future
supersystem state by keeping the target, the intermediate semi-states, and the
remaining residual gaps visible.

The proposed temporal model treats `prefix.base.suffix.*` as a
membrane through time. It would ask what that membrane looks like now, in a day,
in a month, in a year, or across a decade, using only bounded evidence from the
workspace.

Proposed Warp epics and milestones let an expert name what should be complete, what
should still be pending, what remains research, and what is blocked at each
horizon. Long-term epochs can group many epics or milestones.

Warp now has a shipped, read-only core query and composition surface:

```text
recur warp status <lane> --json
recur warp explain <lane> --json
recur warp next <lane> --json
recur warp collapse-plan <lane> --json
recur warp map <warp> --json
recur warp merge <warp> --json
recur warp config --json
```

The audited 837dee4 source also implements bounded companion actions:

```text
recur-warp complete <warp> <slice> --attempt-id <id> --result-hash <hash> --evidence <gate>=<reference> [--confirm]
recur-warp receipt --help
recur-warp evolve --help
recur-warp collapse --help
```

Without `--confirm` it is a dry run. A confirmed valid completion atomically
writes one accepted Slice layer. Identical retry is idempotent; a confirmed
refusal writes a private NAK receipt under `.recur/warp/`.

The supporting implementation and companion contract live in:

- README.CORE.IMPROVEMENT27.md
- docs/main.improvement.27.todo.future-plan.md
- docs/main.improvement.27.recur-ready.todo.future-plan.md
- docs/main.improvement.27.contract.warp-status-v1.todo.future-plan.md
- docs/main.improvement.27.command-boundary.todo.future-plan.md
- docs/main.command.warp.readme.md
- docs/main.command.warp.companion.complete.md

The core commands only inspect scoped eventness evidence. They may count files,
classify trace-id roles, load suffix/discovery config, return a verdict, explain its
evidence, suggest next actions, and partition evidence into a collapse plan.
They must not rename files, delete files, collapse eventness, stage commits,
approve transitions, or start watchers.

Use today:

```powershell
recur tree "main.improvement.27" -d docs/
recur files "main.improvement.27.**.todo.future-plan" -d docs/
recur trace-id "recur.warp.status" --scope "main.improvement.27.**" --dir docs --ext md
```

Useful future domains include synthetic schematics, voltage expectation checks,
robotics capability envelopes, subsystem interface alignment, and production-run
conformance. The command should expose evidence and residuals; it should not
invent specifications, certify safety, or replace qualified engineering review.

The companion implements declarations, completion, exploded-bubble evolution and
archival collapse. General configuration-driven transitions remain proposed;
collapse policy differs from shared query/receipt policy. See
[audited scope](docs/main.command.warp.docs-reconciliation.current-state.md).
Source-branch publication does not attest package-registry release status.
`recur-warp` must not interpret `next` advice as authorization,
execute arbitrary commands, or silently start a watcher.

